  (label "5V_MAIN" (at 466.0 236.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 2debe98c-e158-4132-bc2c-fa8efadea3fa)
  )
  (text "TRIP SENSE MOVES FROM PTD6 TO PTB0 (ADC0_SE4). docs/pinmap.md assigns it as a GPIO input; trip_module_sense.cir designs a THREE-STATE supervised loop and\nchecks the three bands with real margins -- healthy 2.863-2.954 V, tripped 0.310-2.068 V, wire fault 0.000 V. A GPIO reads two states. It separates healthy\nfrom not-healthy and nothing else, which discards exactly the distinction the bleed resistor exists to create: a supervised loop that cannot report a cut\nwire is an unsupervised loop with extra parts. PTB0 is free, bonded out on the 144-LQFP, and Hi-Z with no pull at reset. PTD6 returns to the spare pool.\n\nThe 1.2 Mohm bleed resistor that makes the tripped band is INSIDE the trip module, across its contact -- it is not on this board and is not drawn here. It is\nalso INFERRED rather than measured (trip_module_sense.cir says so), so the band edges above move if the real part differs." (at 40.0 340.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left))
    (uuid 1b48e814-b6c0-4391-98d2-9940b369e996)
  )
  (text "THE FIVE SWITCH INPUTS ARE NPN BUFFERS, NOT CLAMPS (22 Sep 2026, LOWV-CLAMP). The 47k/68k/3.0 V-zener front end needed a clamp that conducts CONTINUOUSLY over 6-40 V, and none\nfits the pad's ratings: a 3.0 V zener leaks at uA (soft knee), a rail clamp parks the pad at 3.9 V, a shunt reference draws 35 uA of bias the cranking-dip input cannot supply.\nHere the pad sees only its own 10k pull-up or a saturated PMBT3904-Q. Checked at the WORST corner, not typical: hFE 30 at -40 C still pulls the pad to 0.03 V from a 6 V input;\na typical part at 125 C does not turn on below 1.3 V. 10k input resistors give 1.1 mA of contact wetting current at 12 V.\n\nLOGIC IS INVERTED -- pad LOW = input active (contact-to-ground channels: contact OPEN). FAILURE MODES, for firmware plausibility checks: transistor open or pull-up shorted\n-> pad stuck HIGH (reads inactive); C-E short -> pad stuck LOW (reads active). One polarity cannot make every channel fail safe; the safe state per channel belongs in the\nfirmware spec. The trip loop keeps its clamped ANALOG front end: its healthy band is the clamp level (LOWV-CLAMP residual)." (at 40.0 392.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left))
    (uuid b5b41e05-242c-47f5-aca4-0cdd812de1ea)
  )
